class.description:
Used for saved entity rows, [NetwDatabase] rows, and [method Netw.sample]. It holds copies of values, not the node they came from.
[codeblock]
var row: NetwRecord = await db.table(&"players").fetch(username)
var health: int = row.get_value(&"health", 100)

row.set_value(&"health", 75)
var hp: int = row.get_value(&"health", 100)

for key in row:
    print(key, " = ", row.get_value(key))
[/codeblock]
A stored name can also be used as a property, so [code]row.health[/code] calls [method get_value] and assigning to it calls [method set_value]. The record's own properties, such as [code]resource_name[/code] or [code]script[/code], keep their normal meaning.
To supply your own storage, override [method _set_value], [method _get_value], [method _has_value] and [method _get_property_names]. Override [method _to_dict] and [method _from_dict] to rename stored names. [DictionaryRecord] is the storage this addon ships.

method.description:
Returns this record's data as a plain [Dictionary]. Override it to remap stored names.
[codeblock]
func _to_dict() -> Dictionary:
    return {&"hp": get_value(&"health")}
[/codeblock]
